This Streamlit app is a secure file encryption system. It lets users sign up, log in, and upload files. 
Files are encrypted using AES-CTR with keys derived from strong entropy sources like user input and system activity.
The app packages the encrypted file, metadata, and keys into a ZIP, where the master key itself is encrypted with a password-derived key. 
On decryption, the user provides their password to recover the master key and decrypt the file. 
The design demonstrates entropy pooling, layered encryption, and session management. 

 py -3 -m venv env
.\env\Scripts\activate  
 streamlit run app.py  
